⭐ Reflection Notes

The project demonstrates the importance of balancing exploration and exploitation in black-box optimisation.

Early-stage exploration helped build robust surrogate models, while later-stage exploitation improved objective performance.

Limitations include:

Sampling bias

Limited evaluation budget

Sensitivity to noise

Future work could explore adaptive acquisition scheduling and multi-surrogate ensemble approaches.

